    "rawPoints": 108.75,
    "bonusPoints": 0,
    "potentialPoints": 150,
    "percent": 72.5,
    "finalScore": 8.5,
    "adjustment": 12.5,
    "adjustmentNote": "Storyline / theme bonus - graded as the album it is, not just song quality",
    "tracks": [
      {
        "n": 1,
        "title": "DustCutter",
        "score": 10,
        "bonus": 0,
        "note": "I like the intro. Broken instrumentals and a perfect catch. The song and album quickly go off of his previous album, I Didn't Mean To Haunt You, if he pulled off before killing himself."
      },
      {
        "n": 2,
        "title": "A La Carte",
        "score": 8.5,
        "bonus": 0,
        "note": "The Pre-Chorus is perfect. The Chorus is a good compliment to it. Brakence is good at what he was asked to do, but I fail to see what his part really adds. I feel like a female feature would have done better. Maybe a sample would have been better."
      },
      {
        "n": 3,
        "title": "Pretty Privilege",
        "score": 8.5,
        "bonus": 0,
        "note": "Good build on the theme. Short and sweet for the vocal part. I interpret the long instrumental to be content solitude. Not caring for any outside distractions and just letting his head create what is lively."
      },
      {
        "n": 4,
        "title": "Easier",
        "score": 9,
        "bonus": 0,
        "note": "A blurred line of what direction he takes with this girl. In this case, that's a good thing. Being vague works for an album like ScrapYard. Attempting to think Rationally about something, yet still unable to get a clear image. It's not as easy as it seems."
      },
      {
        "n": 5,
        "title": "Even if I tried",
        "score": 6,
        "bonus": 0,
        "note": "Misplaced. A hype song is not placed after a line of uncertainty. I can stretch to an added theme of Bipolar disorder, but that's stretching. Also, the last half's lyrics are only a touch about KSI level. Instrumentals are good, but not my style."
      },
      {
        "n": 6,
        "title": "What's it to him",
        "score": 8.5,
        "bonus": 0,
        "note": "If this song came before \"Even if I tried\", the sequence would be perfect so far. A slow start offering some clarity into a heavy and upbeat end."
      },
      {
        "n": 7,
        "title": "U don't know me like that",
        "score": 6.5,
        "bonus": 0,
        "note": "Lyrics aren't stellar, but they're not unlistenable. I feel this song is more of a listen to the vibe, not the lyrics. Its not bad by any means, and I actually say above average."
      },
      {
        "n": 8,
        "title": "I make it look effortless",
        "score": 3,
        "bonus": 0,
        "note": "As a bridge/Interlude, I could let it be, but it's supposed to be a real song. There's no added theme, it's just filler. A vague reference to \"holding the door\" for a girl to leave, but the rest is just rambling that reminds me he still made Voice Memos, and that shit was mostly ass."
      },
      {
        "n": 9,
        "title": "Way too many friends",
        "score": 5.5,
        "bonus": 0,
        "note": "One of the better attempts I've seen at a clean bridge song. A few good lines, and overall doesn't sound bad. It just seems repetitive and blurs into the previous song."
      },
      {
        "n": 10,
        "title": "Guess Who?",
        "score": 9.5,
        "bonus": 0,
        "note": "Closest thing to my kind of music. A lacking beat that wishes to be a Madlib beat. I quite like this one. It's a guilty Pleasure."
      },
      {
        "n": 11,
        "title": "Under My Skin",
        "score": 7,
        "bonus": 0,
        "note": "Smoother vocals would have made it sound better, but the broken, really not pleasant lyrics add to the overall theme, I really don't know whether I think this is good or not. I like the idea of the song."
      },
      {
        "n": 12,
        "title": "Being Yourself",
        "score": 5,
        "bonus": 0,
        "note": "I really don't know. I don't like it. It's really not my kind of music, but I can tell its purpose."
      },
      {
        "n": 13,
        "title": "U Tried That Thing Where Ur Human",
        "score": 9.25,
        "bonus": 0,
        "note": "I like the name. I've always liked song names that aren't basic. Touches on the term \"I'm only human.\" that is usually said as an excuse for them not doing something correctly. Usually used to make the failure not sound as bad as it is. In this context of it being a girl cheating and guilt tripping. I fucking love it. That being said, Intro is too long. That space invader's ass beat is pissing me off."
      },
      {
        "n": 14,
        "title": "Guide Dog",
        "score": 4,
        "bonus": 0,
        "note": "A forgettable song on the album. Not the worst, but not good either."
      },
      {
        "n": 15,
        "title": "Texas Blue",
        "score": 8.5,
        "bonus": 0,
        "note": "Plays off of Guide Dog but truthfully, I think it has a better ending for U Tried That Thing Where You're Human. One of the few songs with a real piano and guitar as the central focus that I can say I like."
      }
    ],
    "best": [
      {
        "title": "DustCutter",
        "score": 10
      },
      {
        "title": "Guess Who?",
        "score": 9.5
      },
      {
        "title": "Pretty Privilege",
        "score": 8.5
      }
    ],
    "worst": [
      {
        "title": "I make it look effortless",
        "score": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Guide Dog",
        "score": 4
      },
      {
        "title": "Being Yourself",
        "score": 5
      }
    ],
    "finalWords": "From what I've heard of Quadeca, this is his best work. It's not my kind of music. I wouldn't choose this over something like Billy Woods. I understand the appeal and I recognize its exceptional storyline/theme.",
    "about": [],
    "facts": {},
